   "heading": "PRESENTING SCHUR ALGEBRAS Introduction Let R be a commutative ring. The (classical) Schur algebra S R ( n, d ) may be deﬁned as the algebra End Σ d ( V ⊗ d R ) of linear endomorphisms on the d th tensor power of an n -dimensional free R -module V R commuting with the action of the symmetric group Σ",
